course: dictionary
lesson: 2200
title: Counselor: one word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Counselor is one of these words. Look at the words around it for clues.
explain: «Childline is free on 0800 1111 in the UK; in the US kids can tell a school counselor or call Childhelp on 1-800-422-4453.» Here a school counselor is a trained adult you can talk to. The words «tell» and «call» show that it is a person who listens, not a camp leader or a lawyer.
explain: The spelling changes too. Americans write counselor with one L before the ending, and in the UK it is often counsellor with two Ls. Both mean the same job. When you are not sure, swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: A counselor is a trained person who listens to people and helps with worries, problems or feelings.
fact: «School counselor» means a trusted adult at school that a child can talk to about worries, bullying or sadness.
fact: Talks with a school counselor are usually private, unless someone is at risk.
fact: In the US, a «camp counselor» is a young adult who looks after children at a summer camp.
fact: Counselor (US spelling) and counsellor (UK spelling) mean the same thing.
exercise: «Childline is free on 0800 1111 in the UK; in the US kids can tell a school counselor or call Childhelp.» What is a school counselor? | A lawyer in a courtroom | *A trained adult who listens and helps with worries | A young adult who runs a summer camp | A teacher who marks spelling tests
exercise: Ella reads that a camp counselor looks after children at a summer camp. Where would she find a camp counselor? | In a court of law | At the doctor's surgery | *At a summer camp | In a palace, giving advice to the king
exercise: Which spelling is the UK one for this job? | counselour | counselor | *counsellor | councillor
test: In a US courtroom drama, a judge says, «Counselor, please approach the bench.» What does counselor mean here? | A camp leader | A king's adviser | *A lawyer, especially in court | A child who is sad
test: Why might a child feel safe talking to a school counselor? | Because counselors only talk to parents | Because the counselor tells everyone in the class | *Because talks are usually private, unless someone is at risk | Because the counselor is a king's adviser
exam: In «kids can tell a school counselor», what clue shows the counselor is someone to talk to? | The word free | The number 1-800-422-4453 | *The word tell, which means speak to someone | The word US
